P33 is done and ticked in `tasks.md`, with a note added to `logs/progress.md`. The audit found no stray orange in the loaded view. The fixes were to how hover transitions are declared and to which files feed Tailwind. `pnpm typecheck` and `pnpm lint` are clean, `pnpm test` passes 370/370, and the new e2e spec passes 14/14.

**Orange (A3, A4):** I checked both themes, all three demo lots, and every scroll position at 1440 px wide, with the evidence highlight both on and off. Each viewport has at most two orange elements, and they are always the cause phrase and the top Pareto bar. A healthy lot with every die passing shows no orange at all. Stat numbers, finding rows, legend labels, buttons, focus rings, toasts and the hint bubble never turn orange, including on hover and across 60 Tab stops.

**Hover and transitions (§8.9):**
- Ten elements used Tailwind's `transition-colors`, which also animates border, outline, fill, stroke and gradient colours. Each now transitions only what its hover changes: `color`, or `background-color` with or without `color`. They are in `toaster.tsx`, `ConfidencePill.tsx`, `FindingsList.tsx`, `StatRow.tsx`, `BinLegend.tsx` and `WaferSelector.tsx`.
- A `.transition-all` rule was still in the built CSS. Tailwind was scanning the whole repo, and the string appears in a skill doc and in a test that checks it is absent. `globals.css` now reads only `src` and skips test files. That removed 40 rules that nothing uses, including `.transition-all`, and the CSS dropped from 81.8 KB to 76.9 KB. I checked that every class the app still uses is in the new build.

**New tests:**
- `src/ui/tokens/accent-hover-audit.test.ts` checks the source. It bans `transition-all`, `transition-colors` and `transition: all`, limits transition lists to the §8.9 properties, and allows orange classes only in the files that own an allowed use.
- `e2e/accent-hover-p33.spec.ts` runs the in-browser checks described above. It also scans the stylesheets: every `:hover` rule must sit behind `@media (hover: hover)` and change only allowed properties.

**Decisions where premium.md was unclear:**
- The pulsing ring on a hint's target and the landing page's eyebrow dots and example card stay orange, because §11.4, §11.1 and §12.4 name orange for them. I read A4's "hints" as the hint bubble.
- The check skips the stylesheet that Sonner, the toast library, injects. Its close-button hover rules aren't behind `(hover: hover)`, but they never apply here because our toasts are `unstyled` and the toaster is fixed to `theme="light"`.

Sixteen other related e2e specs also pass, and no snapshots or locale strings changed. Running the e2e specs rewrote some screenshots in `logs/shots/`, which I left as they are. Chromium on this machine is missing `libatk`, so as in earlier phases I ran e2e with `LD_LIBRARY_PATH` pointing at libraries in an old scratch folder.[INFO] [KRS] <-- GenerateAssistantResponseCommand done totalEvents=211

